  "summary": "A pig receiver is the trap at the downstream end of a pipeline section that catches the arriving pig. Flow is diverted through the barrel so the pig is carried in; once it has arrived the trap is isolated, drained and depressurised, and the pig and collected debris are removed through the closure door.",
